## A fresh run

`LIGHT THE LAMP`, `TRY AGAIN`, and the debug surface's `setScreen("playing")`
each begin a fresh run, and whatever the previous run held is discarded. A
fresh run has the run clock at `0:00`, the lamplighter at the world origin
`(0, 0)` with `hp = BASE_MAX_HP` (`100`), `facing = "right"`, and `hurtFlash`
at `0`, level `1` with `xp = 0` and `kills = 0`, Taper at level `1` alone in
the first weapon slot and no passive held, no enemy, projectile, zone, gem, or
pickup in the world, no level-up queued, and the spawn timer at `0`, as
`specs/enemies.md` states.

## What advances on each screen

`simTime` accumulates the frame's delta time on every frame, whatever the
screen, and input is read on every screen. The simulation is the exception:

| Screen | What advances |
| --- | --- |
| `title`, `howto`, `almanac` | Nothing. |
| `playing` | The simulation, in whole ticks of `TICK_DT` (`1/60`) consumed from the accumulated delta time, as `specs/overview.md` states. |
| `levelup`, `chest`, `paused` | Nothing. The world beneath holds exactly the tick it was at. |
| `fallen`, `dawn` | Nothing. |

The delta time left unconsumed is discarded on any frame or pose that leaves
`playing`, whether a tick opened an overlay or ended the run, `pause` was
pressed, or the debug surface posed the screen, so the accumulator is `0` on
every screen but `playing` by every route.

## Menu navigation

Every menu is driven two ways, both defined in `specs/controls.md`: the
registered actions, where `up` and `down` move the highlight, `confirm` accepts
the highlighted item, and `back` returns; and the pointer, which highlights the
item it rests on and, on a click, takes that item exactly as `confirm` on it
does. `menuIndex` is `0` on
entering every screen, and on a screen with no menu it stays `0`. Every move of
a highlight plays `menu-move`, whichever of the two moved it, the level-up
overlay's offers and the almanac's tab bar included. `menu-confirm` plays when
an item of `TITLE_ITEMS`, `PAUSE_ITEMS`, or `END_ITEMS` is confirmed; an
accepted offer plays `choose` alone, and closing the chest overlay plays
nothing. `pause` is read on `playing` and `paused` alone, the movement actions
are read as held values on `playing` alone, and `mute` is read on every
screen.

## Audio

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
The audio layer is part of the runtime you write, and what it plays are the
produced files `specs/assets.md` lists. Define and play exactly the fifteen
cues in `CUES`, under exactly these names, one per event:
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
Audio plays through the engine's cue bus, each cue bound with `api.audio.load`
to the produced file `specs/assets.md` lists. Define and play exactly the
fifteen cues in `CUES`, under exactly these names, one per event:
{{else}}
Audio plays through the engine's cue bus, each cue bound in the instance's
`initialize` with `api.audio.load` to the produced file `specs/assets.md`
lists, and played from a tick through `world.audio`. Define and play exactly
the fifteen cues in `CUES`, under exactly these names, one per event:
{{/if}}

| Cue | Constant | Played when |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `hit` | `CUES.hit` | An enemy takes damage. At most once per tick. |
| `kill` | `CUES.kill` | An enemy dies. At most once per tick. |
| `gem` | `CUES.gem` | A gem is collected. At most once per tick. |
| `hurt` | `CUES.hurt` | The lamplighter takes damage. At most once per tick. |
| `level-up` | `CUES.levelUp` | A level-up overlay opens. |
| `choose` | `CUES.choose` | An offer is accepted, with no `menu-confirm` beside it. |
| `chest` | `CUES.chest` | A chest overlay opens. |
| `evolve` | `CUES.evolve` | A weapon evolves. |
| `pickup` | `CUES.pickup` | Bread or a draft is collected. |
| `fallen` | `CUES.fallen` | The run ends fallen. |
| `dawn` | `CUES.dawn` | The run ends at dawn. |
| `menu-move` | `CUES.menuMove` | A menu highlight moves. |
| `menu-confirm` | `CUES.menuConfirm` | An item of `TITLE_ITEMS`, `PAUSE_ITEMS`, or `END_ITEMS` is confirmed. |
| `music` | `CUES.music` | Loops from the start of a run to its end. |
| `hum` | `CUES.hum` | Loops while Halo or Corona is held on `playing`. |

The first thirteen are one-shot cues, each a distinct sound so the events are
told apart by ear. Each is played on the tick its event happens, or on the
frame for a menu event, and at most once on that tick: a tick on which twenty
enemies take damage plays `hit` once, and a tick that raises several different
cues plays each of those once. A cue is played by a tick or a frame, never by
a pose of the debug surface.

### The loops

`LOOPING_CUES` holds the two cues that loop until stopped rather than playing
once.

- `music` is looping on every frame exactly when `screen` is `playing`,
  `levelup`, `chest`, or `paused`. It starts on the frame a fresh run starts
  and keeps playing through the overlays and the pause, and it stops on the
  frame the run ends, fallen or at dawn, or `MAIN MENU` on `paused` abandons
  it. `title`, `howto`, and `almanac` carry no music.
- `hum` is looping on every frame exactly when `screen` is `playing` and a
  held weapon is `halo` or `corona`. It starts on the frame that first makes
  both true, whether Halo was just acquired or play just resumed from an
  overlay or a pause, and it stops on the frame either stops being true.

Both loops are reconciled from the state on every frame, so a state the debug
surface posed sounds, one frame later, exactly as the same state reached by
play.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
A looping cue sounds through a single source set to loop, from the frame that
starts it until the frame that stops it, playing its file end to end with no
gap; a cue is either looping or not, so starting one that is already looping
changes nothing.

Muting and the first-interaction unlock belong to the runtime. The game binds
the `mute` action to the runtime's mute bit and toggles it from any screen,
then mirrors that bit into `muted` every frame. Muting silences a running loop
without stopping it, and the loop returns in place when unmuted. The game
stays fully playable with sound muted.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
`api.audio.loop` starts a cue looping, `api.audio.stop` ends it, and
`api.audio.looping` reports whether it is; a file-backed cue loops its decoded
buffer seamlessly, and a cue is either looping or not. Loops are started and
stopped from `update`, like every other cue.

Muting and the first-gesture unlock belong to the engine. The game binds the
`mute` action to `api.audio.setMuted` and toggles it from any screen, then
mirrors `api.audio.muted()` into `muted` every frame. A muted loop keeps
looping silently and returns when unmuted. The game stays fully playable with
sound muted.
{{else}}
`world.audio.loop` starts a cue looping, `world.audio.stop` ends it, and
`world.audio.looping` reports whether it is; a file-backed cue loops its
decoded buffer seamlessly, and a cue is either looping or not. Loops are
started and stopped from the game mode's tick, like every other cue.

Muting and the first-gesture unlock belong to the engine. The game binds the
`mute` action to `world.audio.setMuted` and toggles it from any screen, then
mirrors `world.audio.muted()` into `muted` every frame. A muted loop keeps
looping silently and returns when unmuted. The game stays fully playable with
sound muted.
{{/if}}

## Out of scope

- Network or online play.
- Touch and gamepad input. Every screen is driven from the keyboard and the
  mouse.
- Persistence of progress or settings between sessions. Each session starts
  fresh.
